course: dictionary
lesson: 10511
title: Twirl: spins and curls
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A twirl is a spin. When something twirls, it turns round and round, often quickly. In the sentence «Coco twirls», she is spinning round while she speaks.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Isn't that your sister's dress?» and «Everyone laughs, with her.» Coco is wearing a dress that people are noticing, and they laugh with her, so she is probably showing off by spinning round.
explain: Twirl can be a verb (to twirl) or a noun (a twirl). Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then try it in place of the word. If «spin round» makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Twirl can be a verb: to spin round and round, or to twist something round your finger.
fact: Twirl can also be a noun: a twirl is a quick spin, or a curly shape like a loop of icing.
fact: In «Coco twirls», the word means she spins round quickly.
fact: «Give us a twirl» is a UK phrase that means show off your outfit by spinning round.
fact: Twirling is used in dance and gymnastics, and in PE with ribbons.
exercise: «Coco twirls» in the sentence. What does twirls mean here? | Sings a loud song | *Spins round quickly | Sits down slowly | Hides behind her sister
exercise: Mia says, «Give us a twirl!» What does she want? | To give you a pencil | *To see you spin round to show off your outfit | To hear you sing a song | To be quiet and still
exercise: Tom twirls a pencil between his fingers. What is he doing? | Snapping it in two | Writing his name on it | *Turning it round and round | Putting it in his bag
test: Olivia twirled her ribbon in the air during the dance. What did she do? | *Spun it round and round | Cut it short | Dropped it on the floor | Tied it in a bow
test: The villain twirled his moustache as he laughed. What kind of character is he likely to be? | A shy puppy | *A sneaky villain | A lost tourist | A kind nurse
exam: Which word is a noun in this sentence? «Pip did a quick twirl on the ice.» | did | *twirl | quick | ice
